## How this campaign runs

This is an autonomous research loop. The worker re-reads [`campaign.md`](campaign.md) and
[`roles/worker.md`](roles/worker.md) every iteration and: hypothesizes a change (recording which
levers it moves), predicts the metric, runs it, evaluates the frozen metric + guardrail, logs a scoreboard
row, and graduates confirmed findings to `DISCOVERIES.md` only after independent verification.
Experiments are numbered `exp000` (the baseline gate), `exp001` (first method), then `exp002`,
`exp003`, … — zero-padded to three digits so they sort correctly.

- **The campaign definition (both roles, every cycle):** [`campaign.md`](campaign.md)
- **Role procedures:** [`roles/worker.md`](roles/worker.md) · [`roles/planner.md`](roles/planner.md)
- **Conventions & units (bug-prevention reference):** [`{{CONVENTIONS_DOC}}`]({{CONVENTIONS_DOC}})
- **Scoreboard (ledger):** [`results/scoreboard.tsv`](results/scoreboard.tsv)
- **Working memory / settled findings:** [`results/JOURNAL.md`](results/JOURNAL.md) · [`results/DISCOVERIES.md`](results/DISCOVERIES.md)

## Attended sessions

- **Attended = the cockpit, not by-hand execution.** A human-attended session in this folder is the
  loop's **concierge** (`run-campaign` skill): it launches `--supervise`, watches the driver log, and
  relays steering through `results/inbox/`. It never executes units itself. A by-hand `--config` run
  is for debugging a single experiment, not a mode for running the loop. The same gates apply either way.
- **Steering does not require stopping the loop.** Notes dropped in `results/inbox/` are relayed
  verbatim into the next worker or planner prompt, then archived. The agent acknowledges each note in
  [`results/JOURNAL.md`](results/JOURNAL.md): what it changed, or why nothing.

